From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shikosu <teovidal01@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:59:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] aot: NEON coverage (blocker 3 closed for Balatro); the tests
 lift and compare 1,300 vector forms

test_aot_simd compares 530 integer NEON forms, 154 floating-point vector forms, 534 structure loads and stores
and 89 scalar SIMD / by-element forms with Unicorn, over random and edge-value vector registers. Aot builds
text-mode subprocess output tolerantly. module_validate census shows 0.91% -> 0.02% of Balatro's
instructions unlifted, 88.6% -> 99.8% of sampled functions liftable. The Remill patch is
fork en cours/remill-patches/0005.

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: NEON coverage of the AArch64 -> x86_64 recompilation (NX2Linux); no game data in the tests
Issue: none yet (NX2Linux, branch feat/teo-t7-module-reel)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
